{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Judah was</b> in Keziv <b>when she bore him.</b> Therefore <b>and she called</b> — the woman <b>his name Shelah.</b> For had Judah been there at the time she gave birth, he would have named him. Here Rashi explained in Bereshit Rabbah: I saw 'and she called his name Shelah' as a פסקה (piska), meaning that there her pregnancy ceased — like שלהי פרקין (the conclusion of a chapter), שלהי קייטא (the end of summer). And this expression we find in Scripture: ״לא תשלה אותי״ — meaning, you shall not leave me to cease from him. And in the Jerusalem Targum, <b>והיה בכזיב</b> is rendered והוה בפסיקת (and it was in the ceasing)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The comment cites Rashi by name; per voice rules, the compiler does not name his sources, but here the source name appears in the Hebrew text itself and is rendered as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:51.460031047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}